course: dictionary
lesson: 8956
title: Similar: almost the same
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Similar means almost the same as something else, but not exactly the same. Look at the clues in this sentence: «Knowing someone in a similar situation helps a child feel less alone.» A similar situation is one that is almost like yours, not one that is identical. Try swapping in «almost the same» and the sentence still makes sense, so that is the meaning.
explain: Similar is a describing word, so it can change: similar, more similar, most similar. It often comes with «similar to», which links the two things you are comparing. You will also see «similar in size» and «look similar».
explain: In maths, similar shapes are the same shape at different sizes. Every side is multiplied by the same number, called the scale factor. In science and reading you do something similar when you talk about similarities and differences: what is alike, and what is not.
fact: Similar means almost the same, but not exactly the same.
fact: «Similar soups are eaten in neighbouring countries too» means borshch is alike in some ways to other soups, but not identical.
fact: «Similarities» are the ways things are alike. «Differences» are the ways they are not.
fact: In maths, similar shapes have all their angles equal and their sides in the same ratio, so one is an enlargement of the other.
exercise: «Knowing someone in a similar situation helps a child feel less alone.» What does similar mean here? | Happy and loud | Exactly identical in every way | Completely different and far away | *Almost the same as your own situation
exercise: In maths, two shapes are «similar shapes». What is true about them? | They have no sides at all | They have different shapes but the same number of sides | *They have the same shape, but one may be a different size | Their sizes are always exactly the same
exercise: The author writes «similar soups are eaten in neighbouring countries too». What does this tell you about borshch and other soups? | *They are alike in some ways, but not exactly the same | They are exactly the same recipe | They are never eaten anywhere else | They are cold drinks
test: Which word means almost the same but not exactly? | Opposite | *Similar | Exact | Different
test: «Old English had "thou" and "you" in a similar way.» What does this tell you about Old English and Ukrainian? | Old English had no words for "you" | The two languages are identical | Ukrainian is the same as English | *Both use two words for "you" in a way that is almost the same
exam: In «Look at the similarities and differences between the two stories», what does similarities mean? | Stories that were lost | Pages of a book | Ways the stories are different only | *Ways the stories are alike
